<title>USA: Checkmate CEO quits, chairman is successor.</title>
<headline>Checkmate CEO quits, chairman is successor.</headline>
<dateline>ROSWELL, Ga 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Checkmate Electronics Inc said Monday that Jerry Malec had resigned as president, chief executive officer and company director to pursue &quot;other opportunities in the technology industry.&quot;</p>
<p>The company said its board named Chairman J. Stanford Spence as president and chief executive officer to succeed Malec and assume Malec's day-to-day responsibilities.</p>
<p>&quot;The company will recruit a successor president and chief executive officer when a qualified person is identified,&quot; Checkmate said.</p>
</text>
